WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.320
Anthropic now scans opted in open source projects for vulnerabilities with frontier models and supplies proof-of-concept fixes at no cost. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 198. Andthropic is launching OSS Scanner, a free service that uses its frontier models to periodically scan opted-in open source projects for vulnerabilities. The Scanner supplies a proof-of-concept exploit, an explanation, and a suggested fix in each report.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.920
The company is also committing $150 million to the Genesis mission.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.820
It will make Claude Plus technical support available to more than 15 federal agencies.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:43.760
At the same time, it is rolling out the Anthropic Cyber Mission, focused on critical infrastructure and open source security.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.820
These moves expand Anthropic security work beyond its own models into shared infrastructure protection.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:56.820
Diffu Lora inserts gated low-rank adapters into the linear layers of transformer blocks inside stable diffusion.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.740
By-level optimization trains the adapters and gates on separate data splits,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.380
while progressive pruning removes low-value components to meet a target-rank budget.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:14.120
Experiments on Dream Booth subjects show higher subject fidelity and prompt alignment than standard Lora or full fine-tuning baselines.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.980
The method keeps the pre-trained backbone frozen throughout training.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:23.560
The lossy compressive text autoencoder performs residual downscaling and upscaling along

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.160
the time axis with a residual low-dimension discrete bottleneck.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:33.860
It matches lossless text compression algorithms at 2.24 bits per byte on web text while retaining

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.520
usable reconstruction quality measured by BLU and LLM judges.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.920
Downstream question answering and semantic similarity benchmarks remain competitive across

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:44.820
compression levels.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:50.880
The Galahad KV package saves the key value state of 16,000 token blocks to encrypted

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.940
local NVMe and reloads them bite exact.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:01.500
Loading a block is 2.8 to 4.3 times faster than recompute and uses 8.8 to 12.3 times less

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.500
GPU energy.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:08.800
On Gemma 4.12 billion and 31 billion parameter models, the approach answers facts planted

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.240
millions of tokens earlier with 82 and 98% accuracy respectively.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:19.560
Massa scores each sparse unit by how much it reduces matrix product approximation error instead

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:24.540
of keeping the largest attention values. The method acts as a plug-in correction on existing

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.860
sparse attention frameworks without changing kernels or budgets. Experiments across multiple

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:35.480
backbones and benchmarks show consistent accuracy gains while preserving the original sparsity pattern.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:42.540
STI-OPD uses teacher student policy discrepancy measured by KL divergence to decide when to replace

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:47.580
a student action with a teacher-generated one. A stochastic intervention schedule samples

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:52.460
from the resulting probability instead of using fixed thresholds. An importance weighted

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:57.840
reverse KL objective corrects token sampling mismatch on the resulting mixed policy trajectories.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:03.620
The approach outperforms prior on policy distillation baselines on tool integrated reasoning

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:09.760
and long horizon interaction benchmarks. Lapras trains a student model to align hidden states with

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.440
a teacher that produces explicit chain of thought traces.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:17.660
The student reasons in continuous joint-time series in language space and emits text

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.120
only for the final answer.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:25.340
Across four backbones and five benchmarks, the method improves average F1 by up to 10.79

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.300
percent, while generating 23.9 times fewer tokens.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:35.880
The SFTS context method feeds the SFTS model's response as context to the parent model so

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.000
the parent can use in-context learning for specialized tasks.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:39.100
6.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:45.700
Across 19 parent SFT pairs and 11 benchmarks, the approach stays within 2.2 percentage points

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:51.140
of the SFT model on fine-tuned capabilities, while remaining within 2.2 percentage points

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.040
of the parent on general capabilities.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.680
It can solve queries that require both fine-tuned and general skills even when neither model

00:03:58.680 --> 00:03:59.540
succeeds alone.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:05.000
The Remory Neural Memory Network learns to generate a short sequence of soft tokens conditioned

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:10.800
on the summary that help a frozen LLM approximate the continuation it would produce with full history.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:15.980
On some hey, the method improves source attribution at nearly unchanged insight coverage

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:24.680
while using only 5.2% of the input positions. Both Quenn 3.8-27b and GLM 5.3-flash

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:30.380
show consistent gains and fewer repeated tool outputs on browse comp and terminal bench 2.1.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:38.000
And 0.8B Quen 3.5 model fine-tuned on filtered teacher supervision is deployed in an end-to-end

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.280
grammar mastery tracker.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:46.580
On two human curated benchmarks, the model exceeds prompted GPT-5.4 and GPT-5.6 sole

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.680
in precision and recall under nested matching criteria.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:56.360
Serving cost drops by approximately 16 times, and a live experiment records 15.8% higher

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.780
learner engagement, plus 13.2% higher GMV from new lessons.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:06.560
Sign Rag first learns sign representations, then aligns the encoder with an LLM through

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.000
hierarchical pre-training.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:13.940
Target domain retrieval augmentation supplies instant specific translation cues, and retrieval

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:19.360
utility guided reinforcement fine-tuning balances translation quality against harmful reliance.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:24.880
The method sets new state-of-the-art results on multiple SLT benchmarks, and is the first

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.780
gloss-free approach to outperform gloss-supervised methods on all metrics for CSL daily.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:36.680
Parcel contains 3,396 parenthetical style claims from recent New York Court of Appeals decisions

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:43.900
labeled supported, refuted, or not found. Strongest models reach up to 0.97 accuracy, yet

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:49.200
still incorrectly mark unsupported claims as supported, even when full opinion text is supplied.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:54.200
Missing support is harder to detect than direct contradiction and fabricated but plausible

00:05:54.200 --> 00:06:03.220
citations caused the largest performance drop. Analysis of 127,833 real queries from 6,342

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:09.920
clinicians shows documentation and administration tasks comprise 36.2% and knowledge retrieval

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:17.420
28.9%. The median public benchmark shares only 31% of the task mix of actual use and contains

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:22.800
no documentation requests. Benchmarks designed to resemble clinical practice are individually

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.080
no closer to real use than those in Frontier model reports.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:31.400
Bi-level optimization separates the update of adapter weights from the update of gate parameters

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.760
by training each on its own data split.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:39.000
The outer loop optimizes the gates while the inner loop optimizes the adapters, so the

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.540
gate values reflect how much each low-rank component actually improves held out performance

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.300
rather than training set fit.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:50.220
Progressive pruning then removes the lowest-valued gates until the prescribed rank budget

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:50.620
is met.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:54.820
producing a non-uniform allocation across layers that still respects the

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:59.060
total parameter count. The procedure adds roughly one extra forward backward

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:03.380
pass per pruning step, yet removes the need for manual layer-wise rank search.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.620
In practice, the method works best when the target domain is small enough that

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:12.400
full fine-tuning would overfit, but large enough that uniform low-rank adapters

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:17.240
leave some layers under capacity. Teams facing exactly that regime should try

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.840
the buy-level plus pruning recipe before falling back to hand-tuned Laura ranks.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:28.720
Try the Galahad KV package on a single H100 with Gemma 4 to store and reload KV blocks

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.760
across a 50 million token stream without recompute.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:37.120
Test Diffu Laura on a Dream Booth subject to see whether learned rank allocation improves

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.180
subject fidelity over standard Laura at the same budget.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:46.400
Run Sign Rag on a CSL daily sample to check whether the retrieval augmented gloss-free pipeline

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.760
beats your current gloss supervised baseline.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:52.520
Feed an SFT model response back to its parent model

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.780
on a mixed-general plus specialized query

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.560
to measure whether the context trick

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:58.080
recovers both capabilities.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:01.640
Anthropic plans to expand OSS scanner coverage

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.080
and report additional findings

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.220
from the Genesis mission in the coming weeks.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.580
Multiple labs are expected to release

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.700
updated long-context memory layers

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:11.800
following the Galahad KV results.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.540
New sign language translation benchmarks

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.660
that include retrieval augmented settings

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.380
are anticipated later this month.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.900
Pop the hood on by-level optimization

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.540
and you see two nested loops

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.440
that let gates learn which adapters

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.320
actually matter on held out data

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:28.380
rather than on the training split alone.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.820
The inner loop tunes adapter weights

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.460
while the outer loop tunes the gates

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:34.820
so each gate value directly measures

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.480
contribution to generalization

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:37.880
instead of memorization.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:40.180
Pruning then drops the weakest gates

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.820
until the rank budget is reached,

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:46.420
which produces a non-uniform allocation across layers without any manual search.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:50.840
The extra cost is one additional forward backward pass per pruning step,

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.040
yet the payoff is automatic discovery of which layers need more capacity.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:58.900
When your adaptation data is limited enough to risk overfitting

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.400
but rich enough to expose layer-wise differences,

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:05.220
the by-level plus pruning pattern is the one to reach for first.

